den":true},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"script","hidden":true,"id":"google-analytics"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true,"id":"rewardful-init"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"script","hidden":true,"id":"meta-pixel"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true,"id":"mcjs"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true,"id":"apollo-tracker"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"next-route-announcer","hidden":false,"attributes":{"style":"position: absolute;"},"children":[{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"__next-route-announcer__","attributes":{"aria-live":"assertive","role":"alert","style":"position: absolute; border: 0px; height: 1px; margin: -1px; padding: 0px; width: 1px; clip: rect(0px, 0px, 0px, 0px); overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; overflow-wrap: normal;"}}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":true},{"tag":"div","hidden":false},{"tag":"script","hidden":true}]}]},"canonicalText":"HomeOur ScienceFind a ProviderSystemAge™ TestFor ProvidersAboutResourcesSign In →Order Now →Introducing sex-specific results — trends and recommendations calibrated to your biologyView Sample ReportDismissBack to Longevity ArticlesBest Biological Age Test: SystemAge vs. Function Health & TruDiagnostic ComparisonJune 6, 2025 • By Generation Lab TeamUsed by thousands of people around the world, the SystemAge test by Generation Lab is the most advanced and comprehensive aging speed test in preventive healthcare.According to the verified data acquired across platforms, the SystemAge test ranks higher than the Function Health and TruDiagnostic in terms of customer satisfaction, quality of support, and likelihood to recommend.This advanced test helps you identify what's aging you—before it becomes a problem. It then delivers a detailed report and personalized action plan, so you know exactly what to do if your heart—or any other organ—is showing signs of aging.Choose SystemAge Test for its “Clinical Accuracy,” & “Organ-Specific Insights”Generation Lab’s SystemAge Test is the only test that can measure biological aging at the organ level, long before the disease appears. It tests over 260K cytosines and 460 biomarkers from a single blood test.The company’s goal is to provide actionable, targeted insights for slowing aging and proactively preventing disease.The following criteria explain why SystemAge is the preferred choice for accurately measuring biological aging speed.Generation Lab’s SystemAge reports clinical-grade accuracy, validated across its test cases.Let's look at why SystemAge stands out as the most accurate way to measure biological aging speed.Out of 1605 test cases across six test categories using blinded controls, SystemAge showed unprecedented clinical accuracy.Generation Lab’s SystemAge is built on a distinct, peer-reviewed scientific approach.Generation Lab’s aging speed test is built for real-world clinical use and grounded in a distinct scientific approach.The SystemAge test analyzes DNA methylation patterns to detect biological “noise” across all major organs and systems. It not only measures how fast you’re aging, but also pinpoints the drivers behind accelerated aging.Already used by over 150 longevity clinics worldwide, SystemAge is trusted to catch early signals of decline—often years before symptoms appear.You’ll uncover not just what’s aging you, but what to do about it. Based on your unique organ age profile, you’ll receive a personalized plan spanning lifestyle, nutrition, and exercise to help slow the aging process using the latest in biomedical science.Why Clinicians Trust SystemAge?Over 375 wellness and longevity clinics, and 1000+ doctors worldwide use the SystemAge test—making it the most advanced and clinically useful aging speed test available today.What sets it apart? Unmatched clinical accuracy. In blinded trials across 1,605 samples, SystemAge demonstrated a clinical-grade success rate in detecting aging-related changes—far beyond any other biological age test on the market.SystemAge is the only test that measures the speed of aging across 19 organ systems, delivering before-and-after data to track progress at a granular level. Clinicians prefer it for its comprehensive insights and its ability to guide precision therapies and personalized care.The test doesn’t just offer clinical value—it drives business value too. Clinics use SystemAge to increase revenue through bundled therapies and retesting programs.Its credibility is further backed by peer-reviewed studies and endorsements from top scientific minds:“We are now ready for Healthcare 3.0, focused on prevention. Generation Lab is the tool I trust.”— Dr. Adeel Khan, Founder & CEO, Eterna Health“Irina and her team are taking cutting-edge research straight out of the lab and applying it to a pressing issue: identifying diseases much earlier than ever before possible using genetic markers.”— Dr. George Church, Robert Winthrop Professor of Genetics, Harvard Medical SchoolStill have questions? Click here to learn more.It's Time for SystemAgeWith SystemAge, you get deep organ-level insights and a personalized action plan grounded in cutting-edge biotech. Like most epigenetic clocks, TruDiagnostic’s clocks use Elastic Net regression, selecting CpG sites primarily for predictive fit, not because each is established as biologically meaningful; SystemAge instead measures the loss of epigenetic regulatory control (“biological noise”) directly. It’s not just about knowing you’re aging — it’s about understanding why, and what to do about it before symptoms ever appear.‍Order NowFind Your Biological Age →Related ArticlesGeneration LabGeneration Lab Raises $11M Seed Round as SystemAge™ Becomes World’s Fastest-Growing Longevity DiagnosticGeneration Lab, the company delivering breakthroughs in longevity science, today announced the completion of an $11 million seed funding round, bringing total funding to $15 million and placing the company in the top 1% of all staRead MoreAlina SuThorne Gut Health Test Reviews: Is the Thorne Test Worth It?Explore in-depth reviews of the Thorne Gut Health Test. We break down what the results mean, the accuracy, and if this at-home test is worth the investment.Read MoreAlina SuHow to Check Your Biological Age: 4 Top MethodsCurious about your body's true age? Discover the top 4 methods to check your biological age, from telomere testing to epigenetic clocks. Find out how old you really are.Read MoreAlina SuThorne vs. Viome: Which Gut Health Test is Best?Compare Thorne and Viome's at-home gut health tests side-by-side. Our review covers accuracy, methodology, and cost to help you choose the best test for your needs.Read MoreAlina SuImmune Age Test: Determine Your Immune System's AgeCurious about your immune system's age? Learn how an Immune Age Test can determine its biological age and what the results mean for your health and longevity.Read MoreExperience the scienceDiscover your true biological age with our revolutionary testing technology.Test Your Biological Age Now →Generation LabSlow your aging with the world's most accurate epigenetic test and personalized insights. 460 biomarkers, 21 organs and systems.Order Now →Ask AI for a summary of the Generation LabHomeFind a ProviderSystemAge™ TestOur ScienceOur BiomarkersCareersAbout UsAuthorized PartnersFAQsFor ProvidersPublished ResearchGeneration Lab NewsLongevity Articles© 2025 Generation Lab, All rights reserved.info@generationlab.com+1 415 326 36561701 Old Bayshore Highway Burlingame, CA 94010Terms of ServicePrivacy PolicyTest ConsentResearch ConsentSlow Aging.Prevent Disease.Join our mailing listSubscribeWe'll only send the good stuff. You can unsubscribe anytime"}],"residuals":[{"code":"CSS_LAYOUT_NOT_EXECUTED","detail":"External styles, script rendering and computed layout are not evaluated; hidden flags cover only declared inert/hidden content. Hidden subtrees are represented only by their inert root placeholder; their original bytes remain in the capture."}]}